          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most homeowners with concrete older than a year, a blended melter like Snow Joe Melt-2-Go Nature+ offers the best balance of speed, cost and gentleness. Cryotech CMA is the choice for decorative concrete and anyone willing to pay more to protect the slab, while Safe Paw and Morton Safe-T-Pet suit homes with pets. Keep calcium chloride for the coldest mornings on older concrete.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whatever you buy, technique matters more than the brand. Pre-treat before storms, use less than you think, shovel slush off promptly, skip chemicals entirely on first-winter concrete, and seal exterior slabs with a penetrating sealer before the cold arrives. Do that and your concrete will come through winter with little visible wear.
